            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI tried reproducing, but without success.\n\nIt is highly unlikely that this is a 'mini.icons' issue as it [*never* sets this name on the already existing buffer](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/90ab64f944a5a63a9efebe6735e1f2c6d4db3613/lua/mini/icons.lua#L2155). My guess would be that some plugin and/or part of the config switches to that (unlisted, scratch) buffer and that is what you see. Something like \"farmergreg/vim-lastplace\" fits the description of the root cause, but I couldn't reproduce with it.\n\nWhat is the output of `:buffers!` (important that it is with the `!`)?",
